<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Negasi Krestos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1703</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Negasi Krestos was a Shewan noble claiming Solomonic descent who around 1682 established an autonomous lordship in northern Shewa, in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gondar">Gondar</a> emperors weakened. His successors, first called meridazmach and later negus, built Shewa into a powerful kingdom whose last independent ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a>, became emperor and founded modern Ethiopia.</p></div>
